  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3269ab77e5738674b9fefab358f453ff, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::UIAnimLab.Station
  Code: 
  Title: 06  Targets and Animation Sets
  Summary: 'Which object a step animates - the target slot, a Target Path (down,
    up with .., hidden objects, misses) - and Animation Sets: shared animations,
    local overrides, each player''s own On Complete, Override, Save as Animation
    Set and Preview On. The sets live in Assets/UnitTests/Animation Sets.


    <b>Using
    this board:</b> select a tile. Its Inspector shows these directions at the top,
    with Select buttons for the objects to watch, and its UI Animation Player underneath.
    Badges in a tile''s corner say what it needs: <color=#FF9E5E>PREVIEW</color>
    (the Play buttons, out of play mode), <color=#FF9E5E>PLAY MODE</color>, <color=#FF9E5E>INSPECTOR</color>,
    <color=#FF9E5E>SCENE VIEW</color>, <color=#FF9E5E>CONSOLE</color>, <color=#FF9E5E>POP-OUT</color>
    (an animation''s own window).


    In play mode: right-drag pans, the wheel
    zooms, Tab steps through tiles, Home shows them all.'
  Watch: 
  WatchObjects: []
  HowTo: 
  Expect: 
  Needs: 0
  Style: 2
  WikiPage: 
  Capture: 
  Width: 620
  StageHeight: 0
